WEBVTT

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>Otome</i>:

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.840
A maiden, sweet-smelling as a flower,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.140
a single bud blooming in a tranquil
garden, pure and dignified.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.230
Too shy to even speak of love or romance,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.440
she dares not allow herself
to dream of a kiss.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:34.320
Even so, she is now becoming
a butterfly, drawing closer to sip

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.660
the forbidden nectar of love.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:52.590
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:15.710
"Summer greetings to you, Uncle Tamasuke.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:19.010
My high school is now on summer recess.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:21.930
The children come by as they always have,

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:26.810
and now, with my classmate visiting,
the house is quite lively.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.060
I invite you and Tamako to visit as well."

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.910
A letter from Midori-<i>san</i>?

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.290
That's amazing! How could you tell?

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:51.420
Whenever a letter from Midori-<i>san </i>arrives,

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.290
your eyes sparkle with joy as you read it.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:02:59.670
What?!

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:05.760
Oh, my! Goodness me... <i>what</i>?!

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.890
"Wow wow wow"

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.890
Wow, wow, wow--my goodness... what now?

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:12.350
What... what is it?

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:16.480
Midori-<i>san</i>'s getting married--
she's pregnant!

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:19.400
Now <i>that's </i>skipping ahead!

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:24.280
Early this year, I'd heard
she'd been seeing someone--

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:28.160
a newspaper reporter, was it?

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.660
"fret fret"

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.660
Huh. Wow.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:34.040
It may be a little out of order,

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.290
but it's still wonderful news!

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.340
Right. As her friend,
you must be especially happy.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.880
Yes!

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:47.510
Midori-<i>san </i>and I were together ever
since we started at the girls' school,

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:52.140
sharing both good times and bad.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.230
I could never have another
good friend like her.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.190
Aha.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:05.620
But she says she's moving to Kyushu,
where her partner's from.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.000
She's living in Tokyo now.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:15.210
Since we might never meet up
again once she's in Kyushu,

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:18.750
she wants to see me one last time.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.630
So go see her.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:21.550
Huh?!

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.880
"stare"

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.720
Wh-What is it?

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:31.060
Will you be all right without me,
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:36.230
What will you do about
getting dressed--or meals?

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:37.150
Yuzu...

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:40.780
You want to see her, don't you?

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.530
You'll never have another
friend like her, right?

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.370
Go see her.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:55.790
Seeing her friend's face will give her
peace of mind for her move to Kyushu,

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:59.960
plus the strength to
get through childbirth.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:02.840
Yes... but...

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.930
"Worry"

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:10.390
"worry worry worry"

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:10.390
What? I'm not a child, you know.

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:13.310
I'll be fine on my own for a day or two.

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:17.020
I was alone for a whole week
before you came along.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.940
Hey, I know!

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:25.700
According to the kids,

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.320
the village shrine is dedicated
to a god of easy childbirth.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.120
Apparently they like to play out here.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.620
Oh, really?

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.960
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:47.760
Let's come here when we're
expecting our own baby.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.390
J-Just a moment!

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:57.390
"For Ease in Childbirth"

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.400
"For Ease in Childbirth"
Here.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.770
This is for Midori-<i>san</i>.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.230
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:10.620
Thank you. I... I'll go see her!

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.490
I'll give this to Midori-<i>san</i>

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:16.040
and cheer her on with wishes
for a healthy baby!

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:16.960
Right.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:20.290
"JNR"
"Sakura Station"

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:28.010
I'll be back soon.

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:29.550
Safe travels.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:30.890
Thank you.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:34.850
Tell me--I don't look... strange, do I?

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:37.680
I haven't worn <i>hakama </i>trousers in so long.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.270
Not at all! I hardly recognized you!

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:41.770
You're so cu...

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.770
...te.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:49.820
Oh, yes: As for your meals while I'm away,

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.120
I've asked Ryo-<i>san </i>to help.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.530
Wait--Ryo?

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.910
<i>What</i>?

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.200
I considered cooking them all in advance,

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.500
but food spoils so quickly in summer.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.250
I can't believe you asked her.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:06.210
I just hate the thought
of you hurting for food.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:09.880
Ryo-<i>san </i>was surprised, too.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:12.470
Help Tamahiko with his meals?

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:13.390
Yes.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:18.480
You're asking <i>me</i>--after all
the nasty things I did to you?

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.440
Deep inside, you hate me, don't you?

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.940
I don't hate you.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:24.980
What? Why not?

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:28.530
I had an older sister once.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:33.370
But she fell ill and died
before I was born.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:38.540
When I saw how kind you were
to your little brothers,

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:45.670
I wondered if my big sister, had she
lived, would have been so kind to me.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:49.300
I found some comfort there.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:55.930
You're too nice.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:01.270
But hey, you helped out
with Ryotaro. I'll do it.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:03.440
Thank you so much!

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:08.780
Thought I might just go from mistress
to full-fledged wife while you're gone!

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:12.990
Kidding!

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:17.830
The Ryogokubashi train is about to leave!

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.460
What's wrong?

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.330
I'll miss you.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:28.170
You were so looking forward to going.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:31.380
Yes, but... not to leaving you.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:35.220
I feel the same.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:36.640
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:52.610
Wait! What am I doing?! And in <i>public</i>!

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:54.150
I-I'm so sorry!

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:58.450
Just--just forget that! It never happened!

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:09.420
We--we'll do plenty of that
once you're back home.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:19.510
When I get back, I'll make you
one amazing birthday feast.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:31.230
That was one doozy of
a promise I just made...

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.440
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:53.170
"Coffee"

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.880
Yuzuki-<i>san</i>!

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.220
Midori-<i>san</i>!

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:05.600
Is it really you, Yuzuki-<i>san</i>?

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:07.480
Let me get a good look at you!

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:09.560
Oh, Midori-<i>san</i>...

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:13.270
Congratulations, Midori-<i>san</i>.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:14.280
Thank you.

00:10:19.030 --> 00:10:20.990
"Coffee"
"Café"

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:26.080
Sorry to make you come
all the way to Tokyo.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.420
I should really have been
the one to go to Chiba.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:34.000
Please. Not in your delicate condition!

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.760
Thanks.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:39.130
I've really done it now, huh?

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:41.720
Pregnant and unmarried...

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:45.270
My parents and relatives
<i>really </i>gave me what for!

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:49.890
But he said he'll make me happy--
and this baby, too.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:55.940
He went on an apology tour,
visiting my relatives <i>and </i>my parents.

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:01.070
What a wonderful man.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:08.160
Wh-What about you, Yuzuki?
Is Tamahiko-<i>san </i>treating you right?

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:09.160
Yes!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.290
Oh, right...

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:15.500
"For Ease in Childbirth"

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:15.500
This is from Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:21.010
We visited a shrine to pray
for your easy labor.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:26.390
Oh, that's marvelous!
Tamahiko-<i>san </i>is so kind.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:30.520
He <i>is </i>kind. And he has such integrity.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:33.810
I <i>do </i>have to keep an eye on him sometimes.

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:35.730
But even that side of him...

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:43.410
You'll be staying in this apartment today.

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:46.080
Is this where you live?

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:51.080
My boyfriend will be sleeping at the
office, so make yourself at home.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:52.870
Sorry to put you both out!

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:59.260
Isn't it tiny?

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:02.470
It's fantastic... I love it!

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.970
Oh, and what a view!

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:13.600
♬ In the moonless sky I see them ♬

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:18.530
♬ Tiny lights that twinkle so ♬

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:23.660
♬ There, in those starry shadows ♬

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:27.780
♬ See the shape of hope aglow ♬

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:32.960
Oh, there are shops nearby, too.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.580
It's very convenient.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.380
Here you are: beef stew.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:42.340
Gosh, it's as delicious as always!

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:46.800
I can feel how big it is!

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:55.940
We haven't done <i>this </i>in a while.

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:58.770
We did it all the time in the dorms.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.230
We really did.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:06.110
You're not getting married yet?

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:11.450
Tamahiko-<i>sama </i>says he can't. Not yet.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:12.450
Huh?

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:17.380
I'll wait until he's made up his mind.

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:21.670
What if he never does?

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:24.010
I'll still be always by his side.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:30.930
Oh, but then we'll never have children!

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:33.560
That's right. You want kids, don't you?

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:36.140
I do! Lots and lots of them!

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:44.650
I expected to hear all this
complaining and crying from you.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:47.860
I was all ready to bring you to Kyushu.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:49.990
Oh, my! Really?

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:52.200
I'm so relieved.

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:02.130
Such nice weather!

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:05.470
And after all that wind
and rain this morning.

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:08.050
Fitting for early September.

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:16.980
Yuzuki-<i>san</i>... I'm so glad I got to see
for myself that you're so happy.

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:21.520
Now I can get married without any regrets.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:23.230
Midori-<i>san</i>...

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:28.240
We talked so much,
the two of us, didn't we.

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:31.910
The men we hoped to meet,
the marriages we wanted,

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:34.830
the households we'd create...

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:37.410
We sure did.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:42.500
We still have the dreams we had back then:
unfolding across our tomorrows,

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.750
all a-sparkle.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:45.760
Yes.

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:51.970
Even if we part like this, Yuzuki-<i>san</i>,
it's really wonderful to know

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:54.010
that you're living a happy life.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:55.020
Uh-huh!

00:14:56.600 --> 00:15:01.810
The joy of my lifelong friend
is <i>my </i>joy! Right?

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:03.520
That's right!

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:06.400
Now let's have some fun
until the train leaves!

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:07.400
Right!

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:13.870
"To have friends come from afar;
is this not a delight?"

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:18.580
"To have friends come from afar;
is this not a delight?"

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:22.750
Yuzu and Midori must be
having fun right about now.

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:27.300
Okay, you three--lunch is ready!

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:29.090
Yay!

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:31.590
All together now: a big, hearty...

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:33.470
--Let's eat!
--Let's eat.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:35.850
Well done.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:38.020
Treating me like a little brother, eh?

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.680
Is that wrong?

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:43.560
Hey, isn't it today--
the day Yuzu comes home?

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:46.650
Now that you mention it, it is.

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:49.150
Gosh, that went by fast.

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:52.740
Oh, you liar. You're happy as a clam!

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:55.490
--<i>Stare</i>...
--Spaced out...
--You've had your head in the clouds all day.

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:58.290
You've been thinking of nothing <i>but </i>Yuzu.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:01.960
Yuzu's coming home soon.

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:07.050
I've never been so eager
for anyone's return.

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:10.260
I can't wait to tell her, "Welcome home."

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:13.510
Hurry, hurry--I want to see Yuzu.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:18.260
Do you feel that?

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:21.230
"September 1, Taisho 12 (1923)"
"11:58 AM"

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:34.990
"The Great Kanto Earthquake strikes"

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.630
Grampa! Gramma!

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:52.130
Are they under here?!

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:53.590
Tamahiko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:54.630
Let me see.

00:16:56.300 --> 00:17:00.220
Hey, Shima boy! How you gonna
save 'em with only one hand?

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:02.890
Us villagers'll take care
of our own. Move!

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:06.770
Put these fires out!

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:09.570
We can't rescue you now!

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:14.070
<i>This </i>was that peaceful little village?

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:18.910
So much tragedy in such a tiny place...

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:19.910
Then--

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:23.040
What about Tokyo?

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:27.130
Wouldn't it be much worse off than this?

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:28.210
Yuzu...

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:31.550
Tamahiko--

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:35.680
Sis...

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:37.590
We should head home, too.

00:17:37.590 --> 00:17:38.600
Uh-huh.

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:44.100
Yuzu... Yuzu...

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:50.730
I'm the one who told her to go to Tokyo.

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:53.900
Now she's in the rubble
of a collapsed building,

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:57.110
maybe even caught in a fire...

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:01.580
...or attacked by thieves
exploiting the chaos.

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:06.120
It's no good... my mind is
filled with awful thoughts.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:10.540
Yuzu... I don't want to be alone.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:12.460
Please--come back soon.

00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:24.810
Yuzu's room?

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:32.400
Haru! You made it!

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:38.240
"From Yuzu"

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:39.610
What's this?

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:41.660
"Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>"

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:45.290
"Happy birthday!

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:51.170
I've made these for you this year,
because you're always cold.

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:56.340
I know they'll come in handy
in the coming seasons.

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:59.220
A bellflower-colored scarf and gloves.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:04.760
With every row I knit, I thought
how wonderful you'd look

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:07.680
wearing a scarf in this color."

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:11.940
She knit me a right-hand glove, too?

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:15.780
That hand doesn't even
feel the cold anymore.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:21.740
"I actually made one for myself as well:

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:24.370
a scarf just like yours.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:27.910
I can think of nothing better

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:31.170
than riding together on
your bicycle wearing these

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:33.290
when the piercing wind blows.

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:36.460
Shall we try, once it's colder?

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:40.430
Yours, Yuzu. September 1."

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:43.680
"Nothing better," eh?

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:46.470
Still a girl of few wants, I see.

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:50.770
Matching scarves, though?
Pretty embarrassing...

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:55.110
A matching pair...

00:19:56.860 --> 00:19:59.440
So <i>that's </i>what you look
like when you laugh.

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:12.580
Delicious. It really <i>does</i>
have a warm taste.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:18.550
I'll be by your side, no matter what.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:21.170
And me? I'll be fine.

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:24.260
I'm not that much of a wimpy little girl.

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:27.760
That's right.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:29.810
You're a spring storm,

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:32.730
breezing out of a collapsed building,

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:34.900
blowing out any flames,

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.730
keeping ne'er-do-wells
away with a headwind.

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:40.820
You were tough like that.

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:46.240
I'm the worst.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.990
I jump straight for the
old doom-and-gloom.

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:52.250
All I could do my whole life was give up.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:55.330
But I don't want to give up on you.

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:02.760
I <i>can't </i>give up.

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:05.840
I'm determined to make you happy.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:07.930
I want to be happy <i>with </i>you.

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:13.140
Yuzu, I...

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:15.230
I love you.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:18.650
"flo-floof"

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:31.870
That's the door I opened to meet you.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:51.640
"Yuzu: If you're back, stay here. I'll
return in about a week. Tamahiko, Sept. 1."

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:55.230
We'll come back together, to our home.

00:21:57.190 --> 00:21:59.650
I'm off--to meet Yuzu.

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:04.280
To Tokyo!

00:23:38.910 --> 00:23:44.290
Yuzu, where in Tokyo could you be?

00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:49.510
Wherever you are,
I <i>will </i>find and rescue you.

00:23:49.510 --> 00:23:52.680
So please, Yuzu--please be all right.

00:23:52.680 --> 00:23:54.640
We'll go home together!
